# Batch 2.2 — likeness checks (Emise, 2026-11-21)

Variant stills for intro keyframes 5–8 per FERN-KEYFRAMES-MJ.md, seeded from
the canonical Fern reference. All four are DRAFTS for Emise's and Will's
likeness check — none is canon, none replaces Will's own Midjourney renders
when he makes them. Checks are the frame's named checks from
FERN-KEYFRAMES-MJ.md.

## Frame 5 — River of Pages — PASS (draft grade), one note

Fern front-left, canonical: twin scroll-puff buns, freckles, amber-brown
eyes, cream sweater, coral overalls, butter scarf bow, key-badge, mint
sneakers. Crew present and correct (Wren sky-blue cap + magnifier; Theo
butter scarf + stack of papers; Bea mint apron). Ledger mid-transformation
cart→bridge with one cart wheel visible ✓; his counter reads legibly
("127 / 200") — diegetic prop text, acceptable. NOTE: the river reads as
water carrying pages rather than a river OF pages — at the lock pass, push
the page density up.

## Frame 6 — The badge-check (we never peek) — PASS (draft grade)

The beat lands exactly: Fern's eyes gently closed, shy kind smile, handing
the sealed permit to Mrs. Hen (plump, floral apron) at her round cottage
door; the seal is unbroken ✓. Fern canonical on every anchor. The "Mrs. Hen"
door sign is legible — diegetic and welcome.

## Frame 7 — The Reading Tree — PASS (draft grade)

Fern front-left in the listening half-circle, canonical; crew beside her;
Grandpa (white beard, cardigan, glasses) reading one large glowing page
whose writing is unreadable glyph-marks ✓; Ledger resting at frame right;
fireflies rising; listening mood holds — every mouth closed, every eye on
Grandpa.

## Frame 8 — The wave goodbye — PASS (draft grade), one note

Fern waves straight at the viewer, hand raised, the wave reads instantly ✓;
buns, scarf bow, badge, coral overalls, mint sneakers all canonical; dusk is
warm gold-to-plum, not night-blue ✓; the town behind her is lit window to
window ✓. NOTE: the number-cart stands parked beside her loaded with scrolls
rather than rolling away down the hill — staging only; composition still
reads. At the lock pass, set the cart in motion down the path.
