# Hypothesis H7 — the artists are simply better generators

Claim (to be tested, not assumed): the ranch artists handle key
frames well because they are better generative models than the one
Emise prompted for her own clips.

Evidence walked:
- The Iteration 2 packet record (27.6.9/8.6.11/7.6.9) states what
  the workshop work actually was: "the workshop work itself ran as
  ranch-side CPU/frame work and still generation." The Batch 2.1
  wins are phase correlation, crop conform, and per-frame reading —
  CPU operations, not generation of any kind.
- Theia's Gate 1 returns (30.7.9/8.7.13/9.6.9) are download,
  detection, extraction, and assembly — pipeline mechanics whose
  quality is the quality of their verification.
- The one packet that did use generation, Batch 2.2's stills
  (22.6.9/7.6.10/7.6.8), passed at draft grade only, carrying two
  staging notes, under a named likeness check, as drafts for human
  review — competent, checked, and explicitly not canon. Nothing in
  it suggests a generatively superior worker; it suggests a
  well-briefed, well-checked ordinary one.

Verdict: REFUTED. The record shows no superior generator at work;
it shows work routed so that generation is barely involved, and
checked hard where it is.
